+## 51 - (Partially patched and worked around / improved) Massive seemingly base advciv +/- civ4 issue if i'm not mistaken of many cities entering no production early for 1 or several turns many times during the game early (and possibly later this is why many cities have a process rather than no production, as processes are not available early and are listed among fallbacks if production fails it seems but check to be sure anyways etc): add a fallback cheapest unit production which helps quite a lot reduce this, but not entirely, in CvCity::doProduction
+
+See screenshots and files about/related(ing? Anyways etc) to this issue in this [google drive folder link](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1trFS19b14RsYA6kHc8RT6zFyc36KqILw?usp=sharing)
+
+This is an issue i had noticed in advciv, in example 69.3 of the list issues (i had named it example 69.3 when i was still playing base advciv if i may say but anyways etc here in [this CFC forum post](https://forums.civfanatics.com/threads/ai-city-placement-and-misc-suggestions.695343/page-7#post-16782814) i had made at that time but anyways etc, also available in this gogole drive's issue but anyways etc), but it happened only once at least i noticed it only once, but it did seem to affect several cities in the screenshot, but since it was the turn after victory i didn't think too much of it and said it's maybe not too urgent, although not ideal, but documented it still if helps if i may say but anyways etc.
+
+But while solving/addressing known issue as of now 49, i have noticed this again, but now in early cities, and several cities, entering what seems like no production at all for 1 or several turns. For example, in screenshots 2633 (2) and 2634, kyoto has no production, when anything could be best since it is free to produce units if nothing else is good, else the hammer is wasted.
+
+In screenshot 2706, it can be seen the issue is happening in many cities. Also in screenshot 2694, the issue also is happening in ulundi ai city, so it looks quite widespread but not obvious if one is not looking carefully at each turn in cities, as it often only happens for 1 turn, but not always. It also doesn't happen just these turns or runs but would be long to document all, pehraps uneeded, what matters is the issue happens, and often enough to be an issue, where moscow ai and native american ai's cities are also in no production, not only japan ai's city.
+
+But japan ai's no production happened for many turns, something like +/- 5 turns on a row, so i thought it would be a nice place to investigate and try to improve it, as usual with chatgpt 5's help thanks and trial and error xd or/and other ai if needed or/and i want to try them xd if i may say but anyways etc or such but anyways etc.
+
+Anyways, with chatgpt 5's help and my prompts and such too, i added a fallback code in `CvCity::doProduction` (and a bit of caution code just in case in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseProduction`), to produce any cheap unit we can, so we don't waste the hammer, and the only remaining building was the walls, most likely ssuccessfully excluded thanks to our new no walls if at peace and no danger or such logic (see known issue as of now 48 for details but anyways etc). Also, it is a reliable choice, as at least warriors / ancient macemen in our mod as they are named but anyways etc should be available, and since AI is too weak against barbarians or simply to boost its military (as long as it doesn't sink financially it unit unit cost) should be fine.
+
+Thankfully, this patch greatly improves the issue, although it does not suppress it entirely, as can be seen in existing screenshots turn per turn between 2714 and 2728, which cover turns 37 to 44 if i'm not mistaken anyways etc, the no production span is shorter and quickly interrupts to produce 1 extra ancient maceman, and the same a few turns later, so we squeezed 2 extra ancient macemen, which is very great to help our miltiary and barbarian attacking us issues and such.
+
+Note: i forgot to say, but later in the game, i don't see this at all, at least i ddin't check but what i find much more often in cities doing processes (Wealth, Research, Culture, etc.) way more than needed, so i assume they go to the fallback process, but since this isn't available in the early game, they go no production, but i suspect that later all or most of these process cities are actually no production ones that fallback before fails to the process, at least some, so hopefully we'll produce a bit more units than inefficient processes, although they are not too bad really, they are a bit less efficient choices, especially if weaker, we definitely don't want a fallback process but a unit, so i believe or/and hope our patch is slightly more efficient, but check to be sure as this is just a guess from me and i didn't check too much, but it does seem like so, but anyways etc.
+
+But then i noticed the giant issue, even bigger than this one, is that each time we produce ancient macemen, we end up with less units than the turn before. For example we had 4 archers and 4 warriors/ancient macemen if i remember it correctly, but the turn after we successfully produce a new ancient maceman, we now only have 4 archers and 3 ancient macemen??? Not 5????
+
+So most likely this means we are excessively scrapping, which is a huge issue and may contribute or explain why barbarians capture AIs so early, or why AIs are so weak in base advciv in the early say 100 turns with very weak and unchallenging city stacks.
+
+This is now an urgent issue i'll try to fix, and if not possible, document.
+
+It reminds me of the critical bug of infinite workboat loop we found most likely due to base advciv +/- civ4 old code, which caused cities to be stuck producing and then immediately scrapping non stop a new workboat and then be like wait i need a new one xd for dozen turns until it somehow solved, but was very critical. See about that [23 - (Seemingly now fixed) Major bug of AI cities being stuck in a loop of producing a workboat and instantly scrapping it](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#23---seemingly-now-fixed-major-bug-of-ai-cities-being-stuck-in-a-loop-of-producing-a-workboat-and-instantly-scrapping-it-so-without-producing-a-new-unit-if-im-not-mistaken-then-producing-a-new-one-endlessly-for-dozen-turns-until-it-somehow-solved-itself-but-way-too-late) for details anyways etc.
+
+So trying to find and fix and possibly enhance the excessive scrapping issue, goal is to remain economically competitive (not crush our research or such), but don't excessively scrap, and if all goes well reduce handicap penalties, as i suspect AI production should greatly improve if/after we fix it, and if not possible, at least document it maybe but anyways etc.
+
+As for this issue of no production, not totally improved but significantly better now if i'm not mistaken, so trying to move to the much more urgent issue now and see what we can or can not (or cannot? Or not can? Xd but anyways etc) do but anyways etc

